  "fixture_kind": "public_incubation_druid_mana",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Any change to a land's type or abilities gained by a land can affect the types of mana a land can produce.",
      "oracle_id": "34428f42-03ac-4795-8286-6cbea796df2b",
      "published_at": "2019-01-25",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Incubation Druid checks the effects of all mana-producing abilities of lands you control, but it doesn't check their costs or legality. For example, Spire of Industry says \"{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Activate only if you control an artifact.\" If you control Spire of Industry and Incubation Druid, you can tap Incubation Druid for any color of mana. It doesn't matter whether you control an artifact, whether you can pay 1 life, or whether Spire of Industry is untapped.",
      "oracle_id": "34428f42-03ac-4795-8286-6cbea796df2b",
      "published_at": "2019-01-25",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The types of mana are white, blue, black, red, green, and colorless.",
      "oracle_id": "34428f42-03ac-4795-8286-6cbea796df2b",
      "published_at": "2019-01-25",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Incubation Druid doesn't care about any restrictions or riders your lands put on the mana they produce, such as those of Unclaimed Territory and Guildmages' Forum. It just produces one mana of the appropriate type, with no restrictions or riders.",
      "oracle_id": "34428f42-03ac-4795-8286-6cbea796df2b",
      "published_at": "2019-01-25",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
